From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 220] panvk: keep deferred fragment waits across secondary command buffers
Generated-by: LLM

DXVK 2.6 records the draws of each render pass into secondary command
buffers on tilers.  vkCmdExecuteCommands emitted every deferred
vertex/tiler and compute wait on the fragment subqueue (patches 204,
208, 209), so in Assassin's Creed (D3D9) each pass's geometry waited for
the previous pass's fragment work: 576 forced waits per second, tiler
and fragment work fully serialized.  Secondaries now record which
subqueues' deferred waits anything in them would have emitted (draws
that read images or are complex, dispatches, barriers, meta operations,
events, fragment jobs, context splits), and the primary emits only
those.  Pending fragment sync points are rebased when sync points are
flushed.  PANVK_LAZY_EXEC=0 restores the old behaviour.  A biblioklept
who no longer waits at every shelf.

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (OPPO CPH2763, MT6878)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Dependencies: csf-v11/219

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_cmd_buffer.h b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_cmd_buffer.h
index 9c680ae6..8958fb3f 100644
